From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 70/72] hottyterm: hotty surfaces are layers the apprt
 composites

A surface placed above the text on the active screen is a layer: its
paints go to a store of premultiplied pixels (renderer/hotty_layers.zig)
with the rectangles that changed, and the renderer draws no quad for it.
Each exported frame carries where its layers show, so a scroll moves them
with the cells. A paint that changed only layers asks the apprt to
composite again, through its notifier or a redraw, and draws no terminal
frame. A surface that stops being a layer is drawn into its image again
whole.

An apprt opts in by enabling the store; until one does, nothing changes.
